5,1,1,talk,Toshio,,I want to understand which past projects actually worked for the people using them.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,"I’m concerned about how much disruption the timetable absorbs during construction, and whether the finished rooms are actually used afterward.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,George,,I worry about the staff already stretched thin. We need to see if this plan adds more burden to those doing routine upkeep.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I’m worried about the timeline. Every project seems to hit unpriced issues, squeezing a year of work into the remaining weeks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I suspect the approved figures are fiction. I want to see the actual post-occupancy costs versus the original budget estimates.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, your point on usage is key. We must verify if the rooms are actually occupied after completion.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, agreed. We need hard data on room availability during construction and actual booking rates post-completion to justify the capital spend.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,George,,"@Victoria, I agree. If rooms sit empty, the upkeep burden remains without the benefit. We must check the booking data.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
